# Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in. `wrangler dev` reads that file and nothing
# else does; it is gitignored, which is why this template exists — without it a
# fresh clone has no way to know the worker needs three values, and the failure
# is a worker that starts and then fails at the first sign-in.
#
# NONE of these belong in `.env`, and none belong in GitHub Actions secrets: they
# are read by the worker at runtime, not by CI. Their production counterparts are
# Worker secrets set with `wrangler secret put --env production` and live in no
# file at all.

# The "agents Inc local" GitHub OAuth app's client secret. Its client id is
# public and is in wrangler.jsonc; the callback is
# http://localhost:8787/api/auth/callback/github.
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Signs and encrypts sessions. Any 32+ characters of real entropy —
# `openssl rand -base64 32`. Deliberately NOT the same value as production:
# the two sign different databases behind different cookie domains.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# EDITOR-54, the composer's AI backend — read by src/compose.ts. Unlike the
# secret above, the same key is fine in both environments: it authenticates to
# one account against one bill either way.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# EDITOR-54, optional. Empty or absent means the worker talks to Anthropic
# directly, which is what a local run does; a Cloudflare AI Gateway URL
# routes through one instead. BYOK either way — the gateway adds no token
# markup, and is caching, analytics and a second place to throttle rather
# than something this route needs to work.
#
# Here rather than in wrangler.jsonc's `vars`, and that is a typing
# constraint rather than a preference: `wrangler types` gives a var the
# LITERAL it holds, so `"AI_GATEWAY_URL": ""` types as `""` and every
# `env.AI_GATEWAY_URL ? …` is provably dead code — eslint says so. Values
# from this file type as `string`. Production sets it with
# `wrangler secret put AI_GATEWAY_URL --env production`.
AI_GATEWAY_URL=
